# Bashan OS — KDE's file-content indexer is OFF by default.
# Baloo re-reads and indexes the whole home directory in the background. On an
# older laptop with a spinning disk that means minutes of disk thrashing and
# tens to hundreds of MB resident, in exchange for faster search most users
# never use. Users who want it can switch it on in System Settings > Search.
[Basic Settings]
Indexing-Enabled=false
